# What every reader of fixtures/kv4badn.store must answer (W-ES-P8D 2026-10-30): A REFUSAL BY NAME.
# kv4deep with ONE bit flipped in an INTERNAL node's key area (cell 3726 is the node; its crc was not
# re-sealed). The shape still parses, so a reader that skipped the crc would fold a changed separator --
# measured native: Tree(BadCrc { obj: 3726, want: 3720567729, got: Some(292117295) }). docs/STATUS-CODES.md
# BAD_CRC = 10 on every reader; bebop.bin: kv4.bp prints -10 (conformance.sh maps it to 10).
status=10
# RE-ANCHORED (conform kv4.rs `reanchor`, 2026-10-30): the corrupted cell lies inside the live commit's
# range, so the superblock's anchor (FORMAT §7, cell 9) and its crc are recomputed over the corrupted
# bytes. Before that, bebop.bin's st_open fell back to generation k-1 (`kv.bin g` 5, n=125) and the C
# ABI refused LAST_COMMIT (41) on kv4badf/kv4badd: the anchor answered, not the tree rule under test.
